The diagram shows part of a water-depth gauge, marked in centimetres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (6,0);
\foreach \x/\lbl in {0/20,1/21,2/22,3/23,4/24,5/25,6/26} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,0.3); \node[below] at (\x,0) {$\lbl$};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
State the precision of the gauge and its absolute error.

The diagram shows part of a thermometer scale, marked in degrees Celsius.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (5.5,0);
\foreach \x/\lbl in {0/5.0,1.1/5.1,2.2/5.2,3.3/5.3,4.4/5.4,5.5/5.5} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,0.3); \node[below] at (\x,0) {$\lbl$};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
State the precision of the thermometer and its absolute error.

